       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose.\n\n- **Maximum dosing:** The usual single dose is 400\u2013800 mg. The maximum for outpatients is 3,200 mg/day, and many references say 2,400 mg/day. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It adds little analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the effect plateaus.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common anti-inflammatory dose for conditions like arthritis.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours as needed** (up to 1,600 mg/day). This is a common analgesic dose.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided as 400 mg four times daily. Perhaps that was the intended number.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the original with your attending or pharmacist. I'll enter it right away. I'd also suggest taking it with food and considering GI protection if it's a longer course."
      }
